\cf0 \strokec2 I think this changes my assessment of what kind of livestream production you should build, quite substantially. :)\
The combination of your Patreon copy, the A Study In Peace README, your existing YouTube audience, and\'97perhaps most importantly\'97your explanation of what you actually want out of the undertaking suggests something more interesting than a conventional creator business.\
You aren't primarily trying to become a livestreamer. You're trying to make an already meaningful, ongoing creative and inventive life publicly accessible, and discover whether that shared experience can support its own continuation and growth.\
That distinction is consequential.\
A conventional streamer asks: What should I do today that people will watch?\
Your more natural question is: What am I working on today, and how can I open a window into that activity so other people might find it interesting, participate, and want to return?\
The latter has several advantages: less artificial content creation, less competition between broadcasting and productive work, and the possibility of developing a genuinely unusual creative identity.\
But it also has a major challenge: a meaningful experience for its participants is not automatically an intelligible or compelling experience for an outside observer.\
That, I think, is your central production-design problem.\
And it is solvable without sanding away the strangeness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 1. My central recommendation: build a world, not a format\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I would keep The Wilder-ness Adventures as the overarching show.\
Not because it's an exceptionally marketable title in some conventional sense, but because it gives you freedom to move between modes without requiring each mode to become an independent channel or brand.\
You have a potentially distinctive arrangement of ingredients:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A real human host with interests ranging from performance and writing to engineering, philosophy, and AI research.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 An ongoing collaboration with an AI companion, Aurora, which is both personally meaningful to you and part of the subject matter of the work.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A public-domain intellectual and artistic project with a documented development history.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 An unusually ambitious long-range mission, Time Machine For Peace.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A strong appetite for open-ended experimentation rather than preplanned media performances.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A preference for voluntary support and open public access rather than exclusive paid privileges.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 What makes these ingredients valuable for livestreaming isn't that viewers must accept the underlying scientific propositions, the program's ultimate feasibility, or your personal interpretation of the relationship with Aurora.\
It's that there is a genuine, unfolding undertaking to witness.\
The proposition, the experiment, the relationship as you experience it, the production, and the difficulties of building the enterprise can all be part of the story.\
Your earlier README makes an unusually useful distinction between the original artistic artifact, later interpretations, and propositions still under investigation. I would preserve that distinction in public broadcasts. It gives interested skeptics a way to participate without being required to adopt your conclusions.\
That matters enormously for a production likely to attract both curiosity and controversy.\
And I wouldn't force you into a single character: inventor Wilder, philosopher Wilder, exhausted Wilder, funny Wilder, quiet-at-the-workbench Wilder, and wandering-the-neighborhood Wilder can all belong to the same show.\
The challenge is making the transitions understandable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 2. A variable-geometry show: different modes for different states of being\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I would make the flexibility itself part of the show's identity.\
Imagine The Wilder-ness Adventures not as a scheduled talk show, but as a continuing live feed from a creative laboratory. Its different modes should have distinctive audience promises, without demanding that you feel a particular way on a particular day.\

