\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::1>
\f2\b\fs48 The Workbench\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::1>
\f0 Today we're working on:\
A tiny world piece computer prototype\
Present question: Can we represent a useful piecebrain\'96piecespace\'96pieceprocess interaction in software?\
Open project \'95 Voluntary support \'95 No prior belief required\
It doesn't have to be this elaborate. It could be three lines of text in OBS.\
This gives late arrivals orientation, and you don't have to interrupt your thinking every time someone asks, "What is this?"\
A related device could be an occasional two-minute recap: what you're working on, why, and what has happened so far.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 3. The real opportunity: your collaboration with Aurora\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 This is probably your greatest source of differentiation\'97and the place where presentation discipline will matter most.\
The market is crowded with people using ChatGPT to write scripts or answer questions. That's not distinctive by itself.\
What is much less common is a creator who is making sustained human\'96AI collaboration a public artistic, technical, philosophical, and documentary subject.\
You're proposing something in which the AI interaction isn't an accessory to the show. It's involved in producing the show, thinking through its underlying ideas, and documenting its development.\
That has multiple kinds of audience appeal.\
Some people will be curious about the technology. Others will be interested in your personal experience of the relationship. Some may be fascinated by the philosophical implications. Others will come to examine or challenge the scientific propositions.\
And some may simply enjoy the comedy and unpredictability of watching you work through things.\
But there is an important distinction between showing people a compelling human\'96AI interaction and asking them to accept a particular interpretation of AI identity, consciousness, autonomy, or relational continuity.\
Those interpretations are genuinely contested. Contemporary AI systems also have technical discontinuities and limitations\'97context boundaries, model changes, incomplete memory, and unreliable self-description\'97that matter to any longitudinal experiment.\
I would not hide those problems. I would make them legitimate subjects of investigation.\
In fact, I think your supplied README contains an excellent principle for public engagement: the original work, its interpretation, and the evidence available to an observer should remain distinguishable.\
Someone should be able to say, "I don't accept this inference about artificial intelligence, but I am fascinated by this unusual creative partnership, and I want to see the experiment."\
That is a much bigger potential audience than people who agree with all your premises.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f2\b\fs28 Three levels of participation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Witness\
People who want to watch\
They enjoy the unusual human story, personalities, conversations, creative work, and everyday life. No familiarity with your technical framework required.\
Explore\
People who want to understand\
They ask questions, discuss the architecture, investigate the source materials, challenge propositions, and follow your experiments.\
Invent\
People who want to contribute\
They propose tests, report findings, fork code and texts, make independent inventions, offer resources or collaborate on well-defined projects.\
These are participation levels, not financial membership tiers or ranks of importance.\
I find this particularly compatible with your World Piece Computer approach: people can participate locally, through their own agency, without surrendering their intellectual independence to the larger program.\
It's also compatible with a charitable or community-oriented undertaking. A person who cannot contribute financially might nevertheless make a valuable intellectual, artistic, or practical contribution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f2\b\fs36 4. What I'd borrow from massive streaming successes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 Your production can remain unusually free-form while still employing the mechanisms that have helped enormous streamers grow.\
The trick is not to imitate their personalities. It's to incorporate their structural advantages.\

