\cf0 \strokec2 I would be particularly interested in borrowing Ludwig's experimentation, Pirate Software's clip economy, and Maya's ongoing-institution model.\
But massive growth requires something beyond an interesting show: a way for strangers to encounter you, become curious in seconds, and then develop the habit of returning.\
That's where your biggest vulnerability may lie.\
Your program has an enormous amount of internal context. Its story, language, symbolic vocabulary, and claimed theoretical implications have developed over years.\
A new viewer has none of that.\
You might experience an intellectual breakthrough that is tremendously important to you, yet the viewer encounters two names, three acronyms, five symbols, and no clear reason to be interested.\
This isn't a problem with the depth of the material. It's a problem of entry points.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

