\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 Here's where the practical realities become important.\
Your existing channel is not necessarily a large active audience. But it is a real distribution asset, and substantially better than beginning with no public foothold.\
I would use it first, unless the existing audience is so unrelated to your new work that the channel's history becomes counterproductive. Even then, I'd test before abandoning it.\
YouTube supports live broadcasts directly from a webcam, mobile device, or software encoder. For mobile livestreaming, the current minimum is 50 subscribers, so your stated 2,700 clears that specific threshold, provided the channel is verified and meets the other requirements.\
