\cf0 \strokec2 Assumes $10 memberships, standard Patreon fees, and US card processing. Excludes payout charges, taxes, possible app-store charges, and payment variation. Actual receipts may differ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 So, if you mean $500 in money available to sustain the undertaking, roughly 60 supporters is a better starting target than 50 under those assumptions.\
And even 60 supporters is not something I'd expect immediately from a dormant YouTube channel. Your 2,700 subscribers represent historical interest, not necessarily an active membership prospect pool.\
My suggestion would be to make Patreon support a tangible continuing experiment:\
People can see what happened during the month, what was built or learned, what remains unresolved, and what resources would help.\
That is different from promising that a contribution will advance world peace in some direct, measurable proportion.\
Ask people to fund the opportunity to do the work\'97not to pay for certainty about its ultimate conclusions.\
That is both more credible and more consistent with an exploratory invention program.\
With zero income, I'd also distinguish the long-term dream of a self-sustaining creator enterprise from immediate financial stability. Patreon can grow slowly and unpredictably. Maintaining enough material security to keep working matters more than maximizing broadcast hours in the first month.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

